---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Prose
  title="About Birdworks"
  standfirst="One person, a few printers, and a short list of things that ought to exist."
>
  <p>
    I make accessories for the games I play — card games and tabletop wargaming.
    Everything here started as something I wanted and could not buy: not because
    nobody sells it, but because what they sell does one job when it could do
    four.
  </p>

  <h2>How things are made</h2>
  <p>
    Every part is 3D printed to order, here in the UK. Nothing is warehoused, so
    there is a short wait between your order and the post — and in exchange you
    get exactly the colours you chose rather than whatever was left in a box.
  </p>
  <p>
    These are printed objects and they look like it. Under a raking light you
    will see layer lines. I would rather show you that honestly in the
    photographs than have it arrive as a surprise.
  </p>

  <h2>Designed, not downloaded</h2>
  <p>
    The designs are my own. Nothing here is a copy of another company's model,
    and nothing carries anyone else's logo or artwork. Where something is made
    to work with a particular game, I say so plainly and leave it there.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
  <p>
    If something arrives wrong, or you want a combination you cannot see, email
    me at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. It reaches me
    directly.
  </p>
</Prose>
